s products may change and remains at the sole discretion of Oracle Corporation. Statements in this presentation relating to Oracle’s future plans, expectations, beliefs, intentions, and prospects are “forward-looking statements” and are subject to material risks and uncertainties. A detailed discussion of these factors and other risks that affect our business is contained in Oracle’s Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) filings, including our most recent reports on Form 10-K and Form 10-Q under the heading “Risk Factors.” These filings are available on the SEC’s website or on Oracle’s website at http://www.oracle.com/investor. All information in this presentation is current as of January 2024 and Oracle undertakes no duty to update any statement in light of new information or future events. Copyright © 2024, Oracle and/or its affiliates3Copyright © 2024, Oracle and/or its affiliates“The true potential of AI lies not in replacing humans but in empowering them. It’s about creating a synergy where machines and humans collaborate to achieve unparalleled efficiency and innovation.” Fei-Fei Li, Co-Director of Stanford’s Human-Centered AI InstituteThe value of AI for enterprise is no longer being discussed on just the experimental level. Instead, we’re entering a new era of productivity and seeing how AI, combined with human ingenuity, is pushing past the boundaries of what we previously thought was possible. Today, successful generative AI is focused on solving real-world enterprise use cases. And Oracle has been innovating to build practical AI to help customers solve business problems both smarter and faster. Let’s look at a few examples of how this has been done. 34Copyright © 2024, Oracle and/or its affiliatesSaaS AppsDataAI ServicesPartnersInfrastructureOracle brings AI to the enterprise at every layer of our stackNow the key with these new innovations is that they are all part of our broader AI strategy of offering an enterprise grade service in OCI, while also continuing to offer built-in AI in our data platform with Oracle Database, HeatWave and Autonomous. All on top of an AI Infrastructure based on our Supercluster technology From infrastructure:Built-on Supercluster technologyNative support for bare metal instancesNVidia A100 and H100 GPUsScalable to tens of thousands of GPUsLocal NVMe storgeTo our modern data platformOracle Database and Oracle Autonomous Database-Vector DB-Select AIMySQL HeatWaveTo our Fusion and other SaaS apps:Helping Fusion customers get more from AI- Example 1- Example 2- Example 3Transition to customer stories/use cases:Now what we find is that while there is a lot of the AI tech is out there, customers are still struggling to further solving their problems with the technology. That’s why I want to focus on some key use cases today. 4Copyright © 2024, Oracle and/or its affiliates | Confidential - Oracle Internal5AI InfrastructureGenerative AI and ML for Data PlatformData AI Partners and ISVs Block, Object, File Storage, HPC filesystemsApplicationsFusion ApplicationsNetSuiteIndustry Applications3rd Party ApplicationsEmbedded Generative and Classic AIFusion AnalyticsData ScienceML in Oracle DatabaseOracle Database 23ai AI Vector SearchHeatWave Vector Store and GenAIAutonomous Database Select AIHeatWave AutoMLData LabelingSupercluster with RDMA networkingCompute GPU: bare metal, VMs, KubernetesAI ServicesDigital AssistantGenAISpeechLanguageVisionDocument UnderstandingGenAI Agents:RAG, Code AssistDistributed CloudPublicAlloyDedicatedSovereignGovernmentTech innovations across the Oracle AI stackGenerative AI capabilitiesBy embedding AI throughout the entire technology stack - from the infrastructure that businesses run on, through to applications for every line of business from finance to supply chain and HR - Oracle is helping organizations pragmatically use AI to improve performance while saving time, energy, and resources: Our core cloud infrastructure now includes a unique AI infrastructure layer based on our Supercluster technology, leveraging the latest and greatest hardware, and uniquely able to get the max out of the AI infrastructure technology for scenarios such as LLP - Large Language Processing. On top of this infrastructure, our database layer embeds AI in our products such as our Autonomous Database and MySQL HeatWave with AutoML (built in Machine Learning), to enable developers to add prebuilt models to applications and operations without being experts in technologies such as ML And our application development platform provides AI services such as Oracle Digital Assistant for NLP (Natural Language Processing).', vector_store_id='vs_fra_6rlzawvximl73ac7meipidm9so53r36zmoim3501nkzuan2j', additional_properties={'vector_store_id': 'vs_fra_6rlzawvximl73ac7meipidm9so53r36zmoim3501nkzuan2j', 'chunk_id': '0_9c13646e-4768-470e-bd28-2bb3e5c03560'}), Result(attributes={'customized_url_source': 'https://objectstorage.eu-frankfurt-1.oraclecloud.com/n/frpj5kvxryk1/b/vsdga-upload-bucket/o/oracle/DocUnderstanding.pdf', 'gaas-metadata-filtering-field-originalResourceName': 'oracle/DocUnderstanding.pdf', 'gaas-metadata-filtering-field-category1': 'oracle'}, file_id='file-fra-f6cd3c8e-c197-4859-9272-69d92414286b', filename='DocUnderstanding.pdf', score=0.5979366, text="The image provided does not contain a chart. It is a screenshot of a webpage from Oracle Cloud, specifically the Document Understanding section. The page includes various features such as Text extraction, Table extraction, Key value extraction, and Document classification. There are also sections for 'Get started', 'Resources', and 'Feature' with descriptions of the services offered. The page layout includes a navigation bar at the top, a main content area in the center, and a sidebar on the right. The OCR text provided does not offer additional information about a chart.", vector_store_id='vs_fra_6rlzawvximl73ac7meipidm9so53r36zmoim3501nkzuan2j', additional_properties={'vector_store_id': 'vs_fra_6rl